  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police's Criminal Investigation Agency (Bareskrim Polri) is currently conducting an investigation into a case involving alleged treason, which has led to the questioning of several high-profile figures. Budi Arie, a former minister, underwent a nine-hour interrogation session where he was asked 42 questions by investigators to clarify his potential involvement or knowledge regarding the case. Following the session, Budi Arie denied having personal connections to the primary suspects involved in the treason allegations, save for one individual. In a related development, the police have issued a new summons for Devid Agus Yunanto, a former aide to President Joko Widodo, after he did not attend his originally scheduled appointment. Law enforcement officials have confirmed that the investigation remains active as they continue to process statements and coordinate upcoming testimonies from key individuals associated with the probe.",
